apmond (2.0.0)
  * Add - rewrite in C: libapmon and the apmond daemon, wire protocol 2 (not compatible with 1.x, all access points must run 2.x) [bluewavenet]
  * Add - monitors several access points on one LAN however they are linked (cabled, mesh, point-to-point, fibre) [bluewavenet]
  * Add - AES-256-GCM reports, PBKDF2/HKDF keys from apmon_seed, configurable port (default 2468) [bluewavenet]
  * Add - collector only with an upstream gateway on the WAN, ::1 claim with DAD, back off, takeover after router_takeover_misses, DAD re-check by the holder, no automatic handback [bluewavenet]
  * Add - listen before claiming ::1, give ::1 up when the listener fails [bluewavenet]
  * Add - access point id is the factory (label) MAC, six-step chain [bluewavenet]
  * Add - runs as user apmond with CAP_NET_ADMIN only, in procd ujail where available [bluewavenet]
  * Add - apmond (mbedTLS, default) and apmond-openssl variants, wire compatible [bluewavenet]
  * Add - -v and --version print the version line, as 1.x and mesh11sd [bluewavenet]
  * Add - command line interface with JSON or -t tables: status, nodes, node, clients, forget, block, debuglevel, read_log, bench [bluewavenet]
  * Add - package_version, build_commit, running/installed sha256 and restart_needed on every access point, restart on upgrade [bluewavenet]
  * Add - sender summary line, time_sync_failed and last_error in status, rate-limited auth failure notices on the collector [bluewavenet]
  * Add - extension blocks, VLAN and optional VXLAN on APs and clients, Wi-Fi from nl80211 [bluewavenet]
  * Add - sender waits up to 30 s for its node ULA before choosing the collector [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - the IPv4 fallback uses only the lan side gateway, never the WAN default route [bluewavenet]
  * Fix - a collector candidate never falls back to IPv4, it waits for its node ULA and keeps trying to claim [bluewavenet]
  * Add - mesh11sd (optional): no conflict with mesh11sd (set mesh11sd apmond_enable 0), node id chain shared with mesh11sd 8.0.0 [bluewavenet]

